Infra-cloud uses upstream tools as separate programs in Docker.

rule-catalog.json contains rule IDs, static rule titles and severity classifications
extracted from the pinned Trivy, Checkov, KICS and Kubescape SARIF reports.
It does not contain detector source, source snippets, or secret values.
The shared sarifLeads helper supplies the severity classification.
These projects distribute their code and rules under Apache-2.0.
See LICENSE.upstream for the license text.

Sources:
https://github.com/aquasecurity/trivy/tree/v0.76.2
https://github.com/bridgecrewio/checkov/tree/3.4.3
https://github.com/Checkmarx/kics/tree/v2.2.1
https://github.com/kubescape/kubescape/tree/v4.0.20

Dockerfile.kubescape fetches the unmodified WorkloadScan framework, control
inputs and exceptions from Kubescape regolibrary v2. Each asset has an explicit
SHA-256 checksum. The files remain in the comparison image, not the target.
Source: https://github.com/kubescape/regolibrary/releases/tag/v2
License: Apache-2.0; Kubescape regolibrary contributors.

Trivy, Checkov, KICS and Kubescape rule logic stays upstream. Touchstone adds
crypto-specific relationships and evidence gates in checks.mjs and pack.mjs.
